 "notes": "Solar cooling bound on the B-L gauge boson (blue 'solar' curve, top-right panel of Fig. 4), extracted from the vector paths of the e-print figure fig/bounds.pdf with axis calibration from tick-mark coordinates. The paper's main quantitative result: for m_Z' <~ 10 keV the solar energy-loss criterion dE/dt < 10% L_sun requires g_B-L < 4.1e-10; the extracted flat low-mass level reproduces this. The figure also shows HB and RG cooling bands and the paper's other models (dark photon, Lmu-Ltau, Le-Lmu(tau)); the B-L solar curve is reported as it is the headline robust bound quoted in the conclusions. The bound is an energy-loss (10% solar luminosity) criterion, not a statistical confidence level, so confidence_level is nominal. No dark-matter density assumption (stellar cooling).",
